 34AL c  2019Li41: {+34}Al was produced through fragmentation of a 1.4-GeV      
 34AL2c  proton beam on a UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN facility, selectively    
 34AL3c  ionized using the Resonance Ionization Laser Ion Source (RILIS) and    
 34AL4c  selected by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator (GPS). Nuclei were    
 34AL5c  implanted on a movable tape. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b|g, |g(t) using
 34AL6c  Clover detectors and a 3-cm-thick NE102 plastic scintillator.          
